<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>DiagnosticCatalog.CodeStyle</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>DiagnosticCatalog.CodeStyle</RootNamespace>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    This catalogue ships on the 'codestyle' train, which versions independently of the foundation so it
    can follow Roslyn's releases without dragging anything else along. Declaring the train here is the
    whole membership (Directory.Build.targets); it is also what makes the project packable, what gives
    it an embedded SBOM, and what puts the icon on the package.

    Its own train rather than a share of another, because its upstream keeps nobody else's pace:
    Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.CodeStyle is versioned with the compiler, and a package that
    declares a newer compiler than the one running is refused outright (CS9057). Following that line
    is a cadence no other catalogue here has a reason to follow.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ReleaseTrain>codestyle</ReleaseTrain>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Label="Package">
    <PackageId>DiagnosticCatalog.CodeStyle</PackageId>
    <DevelopmentDependency>false</DevelopmentDependency>
    <Title>DiagnosticCatalog.CodeStyle</Title>
    <Description>The Roslyn IDE code-style rules (IDExxxx) as strongly referenced constants, so that SuppressMessageAttribute takes compile-checked references instead of magic strings. Ids, categories, titles and help links are read from Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.CodeStyle's own DiagnosticDescriptor instances. Unofficial; not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft.</Description>
    <PackageTags>roslyn;analyzers;diagnostics;suppressmessage;ide;codestyle;editorconfig;code-analysis;catalog</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.en.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Authors>Reefact</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) Reefact</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Reefact/diagnostic-catalog</PackageProjectUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.en.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    A PACKAGE reference, not a project one. The foundation rides the 'lib' train and this catalogue
    rides its own, so packing against the project would stamp a dependency on a lib version that was
    never published, and every consumer's restore would fail with NU1102 on an immutable artifact
    (ADR-0007).

    Version-less, so it resolves from Directory.Packages.props — where moving every catalogue onto a
    new foundation is one deliberate edit rather than four.

    NOT PrivateAssets="all": the foundation must reach whoever consumes this catalogue. They need
    [DiagnosticRule] resolvable to declare rules of their own, and present at run time for reflection
    over a catalogue to work (specification §16.1).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="DiagnosticCatalog" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
